WEBVTT

00:04.280 --> 00:05.280
Unbelievable.

00:05.360 --> 00:08.080
You praised AUZA despite knowing
they were up to all this crap?

00:08.679 --> 00:10.119
I'm giving credit where it's due.

00:10.759 --> 00:13.720
They have access to technology that
can turn brilliant ideas into a reality,

00:13.800 --> 00:16.359
as well as the vast research
funding needed to support them.

00:16.879 --> 00:19.920
Putting aside their current scheme,
I believe that AUZA is an enterprise

00:20.000 --> 00:21.920
that's honestly doing humanity
a huge favor.

00:23.719 --> 00:25.760
If you start going on
about some kind of Iron Ninja

00:26.399 --> 00:28.000
or Captain Shinobi,
I swear to God.

00:28.559 --> 00:30.399
Screw them!
Goddamn company.

00:30.480 --> 00:32.560
Why in the hell didn't
they let me in on this project?

00:32.640 --> 00:33.799
Well, as for our plan,

00:34.399 --> 00:38.079
Higan and I will go around to the active
power plants and shut them down

00:38.159 --> 00:41.719
while simultaneously stealing the energy
supplies that we need to keep operating.

00:42.399 --> 00:44.280
- What will you two do?
- Do you even need to ask?

00:44.960 --> 00:47.479
We're going to keep on
investigating those scumbags,

00:47.560 --> 00:51.079
but that means we'll probably end up
revealing all you ninjas to the public.

00:51.960 --> 00:53.000
Whatever.

00:53.079 --> 00:55.039
I'll give you guys
full access to my computer.

00:56.200 --> 00:58.399
By the way, there's one thing
that's bothering me.

00:58.479 --> 01:00.840
- What's that?
- Nothing. Forget it.

01:01.399 --> 01:03.479
Why? Are you afraid?
Come on, let's hear it.

01:03.560 --> 01:06.239
Well, it's just...
I've been wondering, you know?

01:06.319 --> 01:09.120
I can't help it. I noticed
you called Ducky "Higan."

01:09.760 --> 01:11.920
So, are you two
a thing now or what?

01:15.640 --> 01:17.680
- Dang it!
- That's what you get for asking.

01:17.760 --> 01:19.120
Damn it!

01:19.879 --> 01:23.040
Oh! Girl, you need
to respect your elders!

01:23.120 --> 01:25.040
You brought that on yourself, partner.

02:54.680 --> 02:55.840
I don't get it.

02:56.400 --> 02:58.520
That big doofus let the power plant
get destroyed right in front of him,

02:58.599 --> 03:00.719
so why let him come back?

03:01.719 --> 03:04.560
Engaging Higan in combat without
the Gusoku gear would be foolish.

03:05.319 --> 03:07.759
I trust in his abilities
to handle the job.

03:08.159 --> 03:11.240
He made the right call,
so that should be enough.

03:12.719 --> 03:14.520
That's besides the point!
Everything is screwed up now!

03:15.159 --> 03:17.759
You were the one who wanted
to speed up the plan, remember?

03:17.840 --> 03:19.520
Except now the members
of the advisory committee

03:19.599 --> 03:22.840
are on the verge of bowing out
because of your brainless ninjas.

03:23.520 --> 03:26.879
Listen up. At this moment, I'm in
the middle of using this world,

03:27.240 --> 03:29.879
or rather, this entire planet,
as a sort of game.

03:30.439 --> 03:33.039
I exert total control
over people, nature,

03:33.120 --> 03:34.719
and all living creatures
as I change the world.

03:34.800 --> 03:37.800
It's the greatest simulation
imaginable.

03:38.599 --> 03:41.800
But if your people keep getting
in my way, then we're through.

03:43.000 --> 03:45.199
So then to you,
this is just a game.

03:46.080 --> 03:48.719
Yeah, that's right.
A game that I only get to play.

03:49.639 --> 03:51.159
We ninjas have a duty.

03:52.000 --> 03:56.039
That duty is to seek out the most vile
scum on this planet, such as yourself,

03:56.479 --> 03:58.879
and then terminate them at any cost.

03:59.719 --> 04:02.840
Never forget there is a greater cause
than yourself.

04:04.080 --> 04:05.400
Is that supposed to be a threat?

04:05.919 --> 04:08.280
Well, just remember, the next time
one of your people screws up,

04:08.680 --> 04:10.719
I'm gonna make them commit
seppuku!

04:12.479 --> 04:15.800
Imbecile does not know the difference
between a ninja and a samurai.

04:19.720 --> 04:21.120
The time is now at hand.

04:31.839 --> 04:34.000
The Izuna Circuit is
the heart of the Gusoku gear.

04:34.519 --> 04:35.879
It's very sensitive and frail,

04:36.560 --> 04:38.759
which means if you use it
like that motorcycle of yours,

04:38.839 --> 04:40.959
you'll quickly put it
into a bad mood.

04:41.439 --> 04:43.160
And what happens if I upset it?

04:43.240 --> 04:45.439
Then it will never smile for you again.

04:45.519 --> 04:48.759
You have to be a gentleman.
Treat it like it's Mari.

04:49.399 --> 04:51.600
That won't work.
I made her angry all the time.

04:52.000 --> 04:53.240
You got to be kidding me.

04:53.959 --> 04:56.279
So, anyway, that's the quick rundown
of how to operate

04:56.360 --> 04:57.360
and maintain the Gusoku gear.

04:57.439 --> 04:58.519
I'll give you
the manual to read,

04:58.600 --> 05:00.560
but it's better
to just learn firsthand.

05:00.639 --> 05:01.879
Emma.

05:02.600 --> 05:04.079
This is my problem to deal with.

05:04.560 --> 05:06.680
You've already done
more than enough for me.

05:06.759 --> 05:09.240
Please just stick with Mike
and help him out for now.

05:10.160 --> 05:12.040
When this is all over, you need
to find a safe place to stay

05:12.120 --> 05:13.800
and never tell anyone
where you are.

05:16.360 --> 05:18.160
God, I'm so tired of hearing
shit like "it's my problem"

05:18.240 --> 05:20.439
or "I'm the one
who has to take care of it."

05:20.800 --> 05:24.680
Seriously, why is it that older guys are
always acting like they're so cool?

05:25.240 --> 05:27.439
I'm too old to try
and act like I'm so cool.

05:28.040 --> 05:29.360
Like I told you before,
in this business,

05:29.720 --> 05:31.079
your partner's
as good as family.

05:32.480 --> 05:35.720
I have a duty to uphold,
so I'm going with you, Higan.

05:36.079 --> 05:39.360
However, I'm also going to help
the two of you out before I leave.

05:39.959 --> 05:41.800
I know that Jason guy
seems like a weirdo,

05:41.879 --> 05:43.279
but his skills
are pretty solid.

05:43.360 --> 05:45.560
It shouldn't take long
if both of us work together.

05:46.879 --> 05:48.839
Did you just call me a weirdo?

05:50.800 --> 05:52.600
Oh, nice. You know how to cook?

05:53.000 --> 05:55.439
I grabbed what was left in the stock room
and whipped something up.

05:55.519 --> 05:57.519
Try not to make one
of your stupid comments.

05:57.600 --> 06:00.439
- What brought this on?
- Let me explain it to you.

06:00.519 --> 06:03.079
Throughout history, gangs,
the Mafia, and the Yakuza,

06:03.160 --> 06:05.120
have always shared meals
together.

06:07.439 --> 06:09.720
Hey, you care to explain
why my serving's so damn small?

06:09.800 --> 06:11.160
Isn't that obvious?

06:11.240 --> 06:12.920
It's because you never
contribute anything.

06:13.000 --> 06:14.000
Now, you better watch...

06:14.079 --> 06:16.680
In this business, your partner
is as good as family.

06:18.600 --> 06:21.399
You have always been someone
I consider part of my family.

06:21.480 --> 06:23.040
Hey, what's on your apron?
Is it kanji for jackass?

06:23.120 --> 06:25.160
Shut up! You're the jackass!

06:25.639 --> 06:27.759
Alright, Mr. Secretary of Energy,

06:27.839 --> 06:29.519
what's this pressing matter
you wanted to talk to me about?

06:29.920 --> 06:32.399
I want to hear what you have to say
about the power plant explosion.

06:32.480 --> 06:34.120
It's exactly as I explained before.

06:34.560 --> 06:36.399
This was an act of sabotage committed

06:36.480 --> 06:38.160
by someone who got wind
of our operational test.

06:38.519 --> 06:40.560
The FBI are hunting them down
as we speak.

06:40.959 --> 06:43.240
Then I need to visit as an observer
so I can verify the facts.

06:43.560 --> 06:44.839
That's not possible.

06:44.920 --> 06:46.879
I can't risk our technology
getting stolen.

06:46.959 --> 06:49.079
I already sent you records
of all our tests.

06:49.560 --> 06:52.839
I gather that you've more or less
forced the advisory committee

06:52.920 --> 06:55.639
into accepting your bribes
with some saber rattling.

06:55.720 --> 06:57.879
But you know they can't
just ignore public opinion.

06:58.360 --> 07:02.199
I let the trouble that you've been having
in the city slide, but this is different.

07:02.279 --> 07:04.839
You damn people
are nothing but cowards.

07:05.199 --> 07:06.199
Cowards?!

07:06.279 --> 07:09.480
Listen, it's our cooperation that has your
dreams on the verge of coming true.

07:09.920 --> 07:12.879
No, I'm the one who's making your
freaking dreams come true!

07:15.920 --> 07:17.800
You seem to have
lost your temper there.

07:18.279 --> 07:19.800
It's one of my few flaws.

07:20.399 --> 07:22.759
I'm pissed at myself
and those political clowns.

07:23.480 --> 07:24.759
So what's Big D doing?

07:25.480 --> 07:27.759
He is currently at his barbershop
getting his daily fade.

07:27.839 --> 07:30.000
- Get him on the line, please.
- He requested this time off.

07:30.079 --> 07:32.839
- It's on the schedule.
- This is an emergency!

07:35.720 --> 07:39.120
- Shouldn't you answer that?
- Nah, man, this is my time.

07:39.720 --> 07:41.839
Besides, I already know
what he wants me to do,

07:41.920 --> 07:43.639
and I've done
what needs to be done.

07:46.560 --> 07:48.920
Beauty is where
I find my serenity.

07:49.000 --> 07:52.240
There's no point in living, or fighting,
when there's no grace in it.

07:52.720 --> 07:54.839
Well, I hope your boss
can understand that.

07:56.720 --> 07:57.839
Yeah. When pigs fly.

07:58.399 --> 07:59.759
I'm not able to get through to him.

08:00.199 --> 08:01.680
Screw that goddamn bucket head!

08:09.040 --> 08:10.519
I'm very sorry about this, sir.

08:11.680 --> 08:14.040
Please allow me to make it up
to you on his behalf.

08:16.519 --> 08:18.600
Wait. I'm going to go out
for a little bit.

08:19.079 --> 08:20.839
- I'll get ready immediately.
- You can stay.

08:21.360 --> 08:23.639
I'm looking forward to seeing
how you'll make it up to me...

08:24.079 --> 08:25.480
when I get back.

08:30.600 --> 08:31.879
Hey, crow man.

08:32.320 --> 08:33.840
I rarely ever
see you around here.

08:34.519 --> 08:35.960
You know, if I were the boss,

08:36.039 --> 08:38.360
I would have just let you
handle it right away.

08:44.879 --> 08:46.080
Why was he here?

08:46.600 --> 08:48.039
Oh, you mean the CEO?

08:48.519 --> 08:51.000
He came to personally check
on the maintenance status

08:51.080 --> 08:52.399
of Big D's Gusoku gear.

08:53.000 --> 08:55.440
It's the first time he's ever
done anything like that.

08:55.879 --> 08:59.279
- What's the progress on this one?
- Currently at 92%.

09:00.159 --> 09:01.960
It should be completed very soon.

09:09.840 --> 09:10.919
Studying hard, eh?

09:11.720 --> 09:14.039
I'm still reeling from the fact
that she's a ninja.

09:14.519 --> 09:16.200
I had absolutely no idea.

09:16.639 --> 09:17.759
Yeah, I can't believe it either.

09:18.360 --> 09:20.679
I worked much closer with her
than you did,

09:21.559 --> 09:24.759
and I never saw one damn thing that
would make me think she's one of you.

09:26.759 --> 09:30.360
Hey, Ducky, do me a favor.
Keep Emma safe, you hear?

09:31.919 --> 09:33.919
Our target is a report stored
on their main server

09:34.000 --> 09:36.240
that contains operational data
on the reactor.

09:36.840 --> 09:39.360
It should include evidence of them
using newly developed weapons

09:39.440 --> 09:41.840
to secretly intervene
in foreign disputes,

09:42.399 --> 09:43.799
as well as the name
of whoever they report to.

09:44.240 --> 09:47.159
- Who could that be?
- One of this country's top brass.

09:47.240 --> 09:48.399
That sounds juicy.

09:48.480 --> 09:52.440
AUZA's main server is hosted across a
constellation of independent satellites.

09:53.039 --> 09:56.559
Hold on. I got fired while working on
developing that very system.

09:56.639 --> 09:58.200
Now you're saying it's operational?

09:58.799 --> 10:00.279
Yeah, and we're going to hack it.

10:00.600 --> 10:03.080
I'll teach them for laying
their grubby hands on my work.

10:03.799 --> 10:04.960
I appreciate your business.

10:05.480 --> 10:06.840
Now that's fresh.

10:07.679 --> 10:10.080
Your skills are even better
than they were yesterday.

10:10.600 --> 10:12.399
I look forward to seeing you again
tomorrow.

10:15.000 --> 10:16.039
This is the R&D department.

10:16.360 --> 10:18.600
<i>We have just completed the
maintenance on your Gusoku gear.</i>

10:18.679 --> 10:19.799
It's ready for you.

10:21.919 --> 10:24.360
Your timing couldn't be more elegant.

10:29.159 --> 10:32.440
No freaking way!
We've already broken past the firewall.

10:33.039 --> 10:35.080
Stay focused.
This is where things get tricky.

10:35.440 --> 10:37.440
I'm taking back my satellites.

10:37.519 --> 10:39.840
Suck on this,
you goddamn AUZA pricks!

10:39.919 --> 10:40.919
Calm down.

10:41.000 --> 10:43.399
I'll drag 'em down to hell
with me if I have to.

10:43.480 --> 10:45.279
Get ready to burn, you bastards!

10:45.679 --> 10:48.200
I guess it's true
what they say about desperation

10:48.279 --> 10:50.080
being like courage for cowards.

10:52.120 --> 10:54.759
- What the hell is that?
- A ninja.

10:55.240 --> 10:56.240
How'd he find us?

10:56.679 --> 10:59.759
- Hurry and get into your gear.
- He caught us off guard.

10:59.840 --> 11:02.639
Ah, hell! Just as we were
starting to wreck shit up.

11:02.720 --> 11:05.440
Emma, can I handle any of the
weapons that are in the truck?

11:05.759 --> 11:07.480
They all function just like
modern firearms.

11:07.559 --> 11:09.759
Perfect. You two stay here.

11:10.679 --> 11:11.679
Let's keep going.

11:11.759 --> 11:14.799
Next stop all the secret accounts
in the AUZA banking network--

11:14.879 --> 11:16.960
a list of every dignitary
and elites in the country.

11:17.039 --> 11:19.279
The president is going to have
a goddamn heart attack.

11:22.519 --> 11:24.559
Looks like we're both
under the same limitations.

11:26.919 --> 11:28.399
Now, let's do this!

11:43.120 --> 11:44.600
Oh, my God. Scumbags!

11:44.679 --> 11:46.120
We're almost done! Stay focused.

11:47.159 --> 11:48.600
Well, good thing it's so quiet!

11:55.720 --> 11:57.080
- Little fool.
- Relax.

11:57.399 --> 11:59.399
They're not there to ruin your party.

12:03.120 --> 12:04.799
No, no, no, no, no, no!

12:08.399 --> 12:11.519
- That should buy us a little time.
- Just how little are we talking here?

12:11.960 --> 12:15.080
About a minute. Even less if they decide
to use a rocket launcher.

12:15.519 --> 12:16.639
Launcher ready!

12:21.240 --> 12:24.039
Not on my watch, assholes!

12:25.919 --> 12:26.879
Aw, hell!

12:29.519 --> 12:31.399
- Can I leave this to you?
- I'm all over it.

12:31.480 --> 12:33.320
Transfer the data over
to my external hard drive.

12:33.399 --> 12:35.600
It'll automatically encrypt
whatever you put on it.

13:17.759 --> 13:20.320
Damn, Emma, you're never going to
listen to my orders, are you?

13:20.639 --> 13:21.639
Yeah, of course not.

13:22.039 --> 13:24.279
I made it into the main server.

13:24.919 --> 13:27.600
External access detected.
Defense programs activated.

13:28.039 --> 13:30.039
Crap. They're already on to me.

13:30.360 --> 13:32.559
But... it's too late.

13:41.159 --> 13:42.080
Mike!

13:43.200 --> 13:44.200
Talk to me!

13:46.720 --> 13:48.559
Ducky, keep Emma safe, you hear?

13:49.639 --> 13:52.200
The only thing I'm focused on
is crushing the organization.

13:52.759 --> 13:55.399
- Huh? Hey, wait a minute.
- This has to end.

13:55.480 --> 13:58.039
It's the only way we can free
all the ninjas from their missions.

13:58.840 --> 14:02.320
Making sure Emma has a better future
after I'm finished is your responsibility.

14:03.879 --> 14:05.799
Mike! Mike!

14:08.039 --> 14:11.000
Come on. I've taken kicks from you
that have done more damage.

14:13.919 --> 14:16.039
Don't worry about me.
I ain't dead yet.

14:16.720 --> 14:17.720
And besides,

14:17.799 --> 14:21.120
you're the one who said you still have a
lot to learn from me, remember?

14:22.639 --> 14:24.720
Yeah, I remember, boss man.

14:28.919 --> 14:30.919
- You ready?
- Of course.

14:36.919 --> 14:38.120
Special delivery!

14:43.879 --> 14:45.159
Go! Go! Go!

14:50.720 --> 14:52.600
Take this, you sons of bitches!

15:29.200 --> 15:30.639
That was outstanding.

15:31.919 --> 15:33.480
I'm perfectly satisfied.

15:35.559 --> 15:37.799
What an elegant battle we had.

15:46.559 --> 15:47.720
Are you okay?

15:49.000 --> 15:49.919
Big D!

15:50.639 --> 15:51.559
Aska.

15:52.279 --> 15:55.480
Tell me... why would you do something
that's ugly as betray us?

15:56.200 --> 15:57.799
I know it may seem like that to you,

15:58.559 --> 16:02.440
but the truth of the matter is
I never betrayed what I truly believe in.

16:03.799 --> 16:06.000
So you were never on our side
to begin with, then?

16:06.519 --> 16:08.919
That's a hard truth to swallow,
but a beautiful answer.

16:09.559 --> 16:12.039
Okay. Go ahead.
Let's end this.

16:17.200 --> 16:18.399
Ahh, that little prick!

16:18.840 --> 16:20.840
How dishonorable can he be?!

16:38.279 --> 16:40.000
Emma!

16:57.759 --> 16:58.799
Emma!

17:14.680 --> 17:15.880
That dumbass!

17:16.480 --> 17:19.359
- He's always ruining my plans.
- So this...

17:20.279 --> 17:21.200
was you?

17:21.559 --> 17:24.359
That was supposed to kill all five
of them, but it only killed one.

17:44.319 --> 17:45.400
Emma!

17:47.680 --> 17:50.839
Higan... is Mike okay?

17:51.799 --> 17:52.920
He's fine.

17:54.559 --> 17:55.480
Good.

17:55.960 --> 17:57.799
I'm... so... sorry.

17:58.799 --> 17:59.920
Mari...

18:01.160 --> 18:02.519
broke my promise.

18:03.599 --> 18:06.440
Hang in there! You said you would
watch over me until the end, damn it!

18:06.519 --> 18:07.519
Come on, Emma.

18:08.799 --> 18:10.480
Listen... Mike...

18:11.559 --> 18:13.279
Hold on.
We're calling an ambulance.

18:13.640 --> 18:14.680
Don't die on me.

18:15.039 --> 18:16.039
Hey, Jason!

18:20.400 --> 18:21.319
This...

18:22.119 --> 18:23.279
is my real face.

18:23.960 --> 18:27.119
Like I said before, there's nothing
that surprises me anymore.

18:27.720 --> 18:31.359
I bet... you'd never recognize
me if we met like this.

18:31.720 --> 18:34.640
Change your appearance all you want,
I'd still know it was you.

18:35.200 --> 18:37.440
I've been in this business
long enough to tell.

18:38.720 --> 18:40.079
How could you?

18:40.480 --> 18:42.559
That's something
I can teach you later.

18:44.400 --> 18:45.759
Hey, Emma?

18:47.079 --> 18:50.880
I always thought that
when my time came, I would...

18:51.519 --> 18:54.160
I would definitely die alone.

18:54.680 --> 18:56.119
Don't start with that bullshit!

18:56.559 --> 18:59.480
- You're not going to die here!
- Emma! Live on!

19:01.519 --> 19:04.599
I'm so lucky, baby

19:06.480 --> 19:11.960
<i>'Cause you are...
my girlfriend</i>

19:13.839 --> 19:14.960
Hey.

19:20.440 --> 19:23.119
This is precious to you, right?
Don't go losing it.

19:23.839 --> 19:25.359
Oh, yeah. Thank you.

19:27.559 --> 19:30.119
You know, I think
he kind of looks like you.

19:30.200 --> 19:31.640
I think you had
way too much to drink!

19:43.000 --> 19:45.240
I'm so lucky, baby

19:46.319 --> 19:50.519
'Cause you are my girlfriend

19:51.160 --> 19:52.279
Don't laugh at me!

19:52.880 --> 19:58.920
<i>And maybe
You're my one and only</i>

20:01.480 --> 20:03.079
Tell me...

20:07.079 --> 20:08.160
Emma.

20:09.079 --> 20:10.119
Emma!

20:12.200 --> 20:13.160
Emma...

20:19.279 --> 20:22.759
She was the biggest pain in the ass
that I ever had the pleasure to work with.

20:22.839 --> 20:25.400
Always showed up late,
never listened.

20:26.000 --> 20:29.240
At some point, I found myself
thinking that talking with her

20:29.559 --> 20:32.599
was what it might feel like
if my daughter was still alive.

20:33.759 --> 20:36.240
So to me, Emma was like...

20:37.000 --> 20:39.079
having another chance
with my daughter.

20:40.599 --> 20:44.240
But... there was a guilt
that came with it.

20:45.920 --> 20:47.279
I felt like I could never tell her.

20:49.640 --> 20:52.240
Why would you ever think
you were going to die alone?

20:52.319 --> 20:53.319
Stupid girl.

20:55.880 --> 20:58.079
Damn it!
I should have just told her how I felt.

20:58.640 --> 21:00.400
Even if you never said it, she knew.

21:01.279 --> 21:04.200
I've never seen a ninja die with
that kind of look on their face.

21:25.000 --> 21:26.920
I'm going to tear
the organization to pieces.

21:28.240 --> 21:31.680
<i>Whenever Mari fought,
her goal was always to defend.</i>

21:47.440 --> 21:49.559
It's time to put an end to this.

22:08.000 --> 22:12.920
Revised and Synchronized by
FAST TITLES MEDIA
